{
  "_about": {
    "what": "Scoring rules for ranking PSI test configurations against a user scenario. Read by scoring/scorer.py; the dashboard can read the same file (e.g., to draw weight sliders).",
    "status": "Team proposal (2026-11-14), not NASA guidance. Config 1.4.0: the profile weights come from scoring/derive_weights.py, which combines the streams named in scoring/weight_streams.json. Judgement stream: AHP over literature-based pairwise judgements, filled in by an AI session from evidence classes with cited textbooks, papers and NASA records (scoring/literature_evidence.json; CR 0, 0.009 and 0.008). Suppression is further pooled, over o2, pressure, diluent and fuel, with the relative importance of those conditions in the NASA FLEX measurements (scoring/data_weights.json). The human lead approved the AHP (19:26), the FLEX pooling (20:06) and the literature stream (20:19). All other values are unchanged from 1.1.0 and were approved after the AI review in scoring/PARAMETER_REVIEW.md. The model's build-up and its sources are in scoring/BUILDUP.md. Change values here only, never in code; change the weights only through the stream files and derive_weights.py --write.",
    "generated_by": "AI-assisted (Claude), reviewed: profile weights of 1.0.0-1.1.0 (direct point allocation) approved as-is by the human lead (team member), 2026-11-14 16:51 KST; all other values approved as-is by the same reviewer, 2026-11-14 17:03 KST, after the AI review in scoring/PARAMETER_REVIEW.md; config 1.2.0 (2026-11-14 19:26 KST): profile weights replaced by the AHP derivation, pairwise judgements approved as-is and applied by decision of the same reviewer; config 1.3.0 (2026-11-14 20:06 KST): suppression weights pooled with the NASA FLEX data stream, by decision of the same reviewer; config 1.4.0 (2026-11-14 20:19 KST): judgement stream replaced by the literature-based judgements, by decision of the same reviewer",
    "formula": "score = 100 * M * G * sum_i(w_i * S_i) over active dimensions; weights renormalized to sum 1 over active dimensions"
  },
